WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.500
Ghostbusters 2, the slime is rising fast, who you gonna call?

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:30.800
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:31.920
I'm Mike.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:33.280
I'm Sean.

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:35.540
And I'm Joe.

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:37.720
Joe, did that freak you out a little bit?

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:45.680
Yeah, that's just, it's just, I'm comfortable now with the pace and the tone and the cadence of that opening.

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:55.480
Well, it is spooky season, both in the time that people listen to this episode and, you know, hey, it's 2023, so it's always spooky season now.

00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:06.420
I'm so excited. Where does Ghostbusters, forget about, you know, the debate between the original and Ghostbusters 2, where does Ghostbusters fall into your Halloween movie lineup?

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:08.460
Is that in your rotation every year?

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:11.140
Is that like a, I don't even think about Ghostbusters anymore?

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:12.160
It's not cool anymore?

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:17.280
Or is that like a, yeah, I enjoyed it and I'll put it if somebody, I'll watch it if somebody puts it on.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:20.500
It's probably the latter most for me.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:26.720
I think I saw Ghostbusters for the first time when I was maybe like 20.

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:40.400
And then I, I saw it most recently, maybe five or six years ago, or whenever, maybe whenever we recorded the episode for the first one, I might have like skimmed it.

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:43.040
But I don't really think about Ghostbusters that much.

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:46.240
I'm not certain that I've ever seen it all the way through.

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:52.180
Like I've maybe seen clips, I've seen like the Stay Puft Marshmallow thing and maybe a couple other clips.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:55.860
Maybe I saw it all the way through when I was a kid and don't remember any of it.

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:57.960
But yeah, I don't think I've seen it.

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:01.220
Ghostbusters 1 is a movie I'm very familiar with.

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:02.280
Seen it many times.

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:07.580
Even at an early age, it was one of those things where like as a kid, you're convinced that it is a little scary.

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:09.060
And then you watch the whole movie.

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:14.860
And even though nothing scary, scary happens, there are some like moments that would terrify a young child.

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:19.320
Yeah. And so it has like that, it's that Halloween friendly vibe to it.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:25.520
Whereas like, you know, you're not watching The Conjuring or something, you know, The Exorcist.

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:26.740
You're watching Hocus Pocus.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:31.960
Yeah, exactly. It's like, oh, you know, it's I am spooked a little bit, but I can still watch the whole movie.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:34.900
The Ring is not something I could do when I was a kid.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:36.140
I couldn't watch that whole movie.

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:38.020
I was freaked out when she came out of the TV.

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:41.900
It did happen. Anyway, this is not a Halloween movie recap episode.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:43.580
This is about Ghostbusters 2.

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:47.140
And believe it or not, we have played Ghostbusters 1.

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:51.000
And I have to say, believe it or not, because sometimes you don't play the first game.

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:53.920
Goonies 2. We never played the first Goonies game.

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:57.340
So for Ghostbusters, we did play a Ghostbusters game.

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:59.440
But was it really based on the movie?

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:14.060
No, it was a franchise simulator where you opened up your own Ghostbusters in your town and had to manage money and, you know, fight ghosts and make money to buy new parts and stuff like that.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.120
Deal with the national gas shortage.

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:19.420
Yeah, Sean had a lot of amusing takes on the episode and everything.

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:28.980
So Ghostbusters 2, not the video game we thought, but I think also for a lot of people, Ghostbusters 2 was not the movie they hoped for.

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:31.250
So maybe the Ghostbusters...

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:32.860
They're trying to stick with that, yeah.

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:36.740
Yeah, yeah, they're trying to stick with that and flip our expectations a little bit.

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:39.340
So, here's the thing.

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:41.240
So I haven't seen Ghostbusters 2.

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:45.800
Can you give me like a 30 second pitch?

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:47.540
No. Okay.

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:57.600
I can give you the quick pitch is that the ghost, you know, like on the logo for Ghostbusters, you know, with the sensor sign going through him.

00:03:57.680 --> 00:03:58.940
Sure, yeah. Yeah.

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:02.140
Can you give me that? Yeah, he has the peace sign this time for two.

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:03.140
That's true.

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:04.180
That's how you get it. I know that.

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:07.900
I do know that. I just thought maybe you knew what happened in the movie is all.

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:13.480
Well, is what happened in the movie related to this little opening text you get?

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:14.500
I am Valdo?

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:15.660
At the stroke of midnight.

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:18.080
Huh? I am Valdo?

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:22.000
Yeah. Like maybe that's, maybe this is a good synopsis.

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:25.720
Okay. But I don't know, did you guys read this synopsis at the beginning?

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:32.240
Yeah. No, I, is that the one that happens after the Ghostbusters car tells you that they're back and ready to believe you?

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:50.220
No, this is, well, yes, but also if you, if it wants the story, you to read the story, it does not make it easy to do so because you have to watch, yes, this, this, um, this cut scene without interrupting it, without touching a button where it tells you that Ghostbusters are back and they're ready to believe you.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:53.680
And it's just a cut scene of someone playing a level for a minute and 22 seconds.

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:59.720
Then the credits roll and you have to watch the entirety of the credits.

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:02.040
Then you get the plot.

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:05.840
That's pretty wild. If you, if you touch any button, you skip it all.

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:06.960
That's pretty insane.

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:12.300
I, yeah, I only saw it after I was looking for more footage to watch.

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:19.260
Uh, not so much when I was playing because I would never be that crazy to wait that long to press play.

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:34.140
Uh, so look how well the game translates the plot of Ghostbusters to, I guess, is anybody's call, but yes, it is following the same, um, movie points of like, it's, you know, New Year's Eve and they, before midnight and everything.

00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:37.580
And you gotta, uh, with Vigo, you gotta take him down.

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:39.000
He's in the painting and everything.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:41.920
All those things happen in both the game and in the movie.

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:45.420
The game is though missing a few plot points, but whatever.

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:50.900
It, it, it's enough to satisfy, I think, on a way that Ghostbusters 1 just wasn't, right?

00:05:51.140 --> 00:05:57.420
Does, does the Statue of Liberty swim and, uh, shoot birds in the movie?

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:02.880
I don't know if they shoot birds, but yes, they do control the Statue of Liberty in the movie.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:04.560
Oh, cool. Yeah, absolutely.

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:06.180
Hmm. I should watch that movie.

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:07.780
That's what sold you on it.

00:06:07.780 --> 00:06:18.720
Yes. The Statue of Liberty being like the thing that they control is probably, you know, like a direct, like, what's our, what's our Stay Puft Marshmallow moment of this movie, you know?

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:24.340
So, last time the Stay Puft Marshmallow was like, you know, don't think of anything, don't think of anything.

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:25.620
And that's what he thought of.

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:28.280
So then it roams the streets and causes terror.

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:33.220
This time they control the Statue of Liberty and all the citizens love it.

00:06:33.220 --> 00:06:44.600
Yeah, because, I mean, everyone has always fantasized about Lady Liberty and just seeing her, like, you know, able to walk around, shoot stuff with the torch.

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:48.760
Like, that's sort of just like, uh, that's what you want to see.

00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:55.140
I'd like to dedicate this next song to a woman that's over 50 feet tall and a hundred years old.

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:57.760
That's another Simpsons joke.

00:06:57.940 --> 00:06:59.360
Just in case anybody's racking them up.

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:00.300
I figured you'd know.

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:04.840
Yep, the next line in that, the punchline is, is that this giant woman will kill us all.

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:06.180
And then the guy jumps off the boat.

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:08.600
Um, he's not aware that he's talking about the statue.

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:10.780
Ah. Hmm.

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:13.720
Uh, and, but look, okay, forget about the plot.

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:15.540
Forget about the game and everything, because it's important.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:19.300
Forget about the game. Forget about, just forget about this podcast.

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:20.800
This is about painting now.

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:25.260
Yeah. Forget about all that, because I think what's important is, is that when you start this game,

00:07:25.260 --> 00:07:30.660
it's immediately apparent that you are playing as the four Ghostbusters in platforming levels,

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:37.400
and then you're riding around in the ectomobile, and you're even controlling the Statue of Liberty.

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:46.380
Yes. Whether those things are pulled off successfully, I think a lot of Ghostbusters fans are automatically, um, satisfied,

00:07:47.060 --> 00:07:57.860
compared to the first game that was rather confusing, and then ended with like a, you know, chugging up the stairs that took forever to face off against the Stay Puft Marshmallow.

00:07:57.860 --> 00:08:00.680
Like, this has more direct action going on.

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:06.800
I'll, I'll say that even, you know, before we even get into like, if any of it actually worked or was fun,

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:11.640
right off the bat, the vibe I get from this game is, is like, fun.

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:19.960
Like, they're trying to be fun, they got the music going, you got like, funny things happening, there's like, you know, it's like, it's action-y, and it's moving.

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:23.460
So like, like, I just get a fun vibe from this game.

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:30.480
There's messages coming to you on the like, opening cutscene, of like, the Ghostbusters are back and ready to believe you and stuff like that.

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:40.020
You got to kind of like, wait to watch the whole thing to get the full message, and it, like, it seems like they, they took a big note from the first one, like, hey, this isn't like, action-packed enough.

00:08:40.360 --> 00:08:42.960
And like, the vibe is there immediately to me.

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:52.240
Yeah, it was almost as if in the first game that they wanted to make a game where it, it was just everything that happened between the scenes in the movie.

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:58.180
Yeah. Like, oh, well, we'll just put all the time where they're like driving to places in the game so that it all makes sense in the end.

00:08:58.320 --> 00:09:00.620
And then, you know, running up the stairs, yada, yada.

00:09:01.480 --> 00:09:16.880
And then an executive was like, wait a second, why did we do that when we could have had a perfectly, I mean, it's not, it's not a perfectly fine action game, but it's at least more.

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:18.700
A perfectly fine concept for an action game.

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:23.480
Yeah, it looks like an action game now, and it plays kind of like an action game now.

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:34.140
So, yeah. Yeah, I don't know what their devices are called, but the slime blowers, I don't know, whatever it is.

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:35.220
We'll go a slime blower.

00:09:35.360 --> 00:09:44.580
Yeah, okay. Those devices that they use are one of the, like, you know, in the history of IPs, ripe for video game kind of things.

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:46.000
It's like lightsabers, right?

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:53.720
Like, it's the kind of thing that, like, sure, just make that the gun and make a whole game around capturing or shooting at ghosts.

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:56.020
And, you know, that there can be a video game there.

00:09:56.120 --> 00:10:00.020
Just like how everybody wants to be Luke Skywalker with a lightsaber.

00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:05.700
I'm sure kids when Ghostbusters 2 came out also wanted to use that to bust some ghosts.

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:13.440
Now that they're able to do that in this one, you know, via action side-scrolling stages, how does it work?

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:22.220
So, all right, you get dropped into the darkness.

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:25.200
You get dropped into the sewer slash subway system.

00:10:26.440 --> 00:10:28.320
And I think this happens in the movie.

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:32.500
There is just a tiny spider that forces you to go in one direction.

00:10:32.500 --> 00:10:37.740
And if you try to go in the other direction, you will get knocked to the ground and you can't go.

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:39.920
I don't know what that was about.

00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:43.220
It's also in the opposite direction that you would normally go in a side-scroller.

00:10:43.220 --> 00:10:44.280
So it's just very strange.

00:10:44.460 --> 00:10:46.320
You're going left a lot in this game.

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:49.720
Don't know what the actual reason for that is.

00:10:50.140 --> 00:11:00.520
Anyway, then you use your kind of impressive, in terms of physical simulation sense, gun.

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:01.740
What would you call it?

00:11:01.820 --> 00:11:02.760
The slime gun?

00:11:02.960 --> 00:11:03.880
Slime buster? No.

00:11:04.280 --> 00:11:05.220
Slime buster.

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:10.480
Um, and you can just, like, shoot a bunch of slime everywhere you go.

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:14.600
And it just will continue to exist in the world.

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:19.980
Uh, you can shoot straight up and then it'll fall right on your head maybe, like, ten seconds later.

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:21.360
It's, it's strange.

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:22.200
It's very strange.

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:28.400
But you've got ghosts and stuff and, I guess, like, poltergeists coming at you.

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:32.120
Some of them you're going to want to just, like, shoot them with the slime.

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:36.360
Some of them you're going to want to put the, uh, what do you call it?

00:11:36.440 --> 00:11:41.600
The, uh, the little robot that, Roomba.

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:46.740
You want to put the Roomba down and then it'll suck up the ghost and you get extra points for that.

00:11:46.740 --> 00:11:57.520
Um, so, you're already incorporating the, the, the iconic devices from the movie better in the first, like, 40 seconds of the game.

00:11:57.660 --> 00:12:00.120
It's still a very strange experience.

00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:04.480
Uh, and it feels like no other game I've played on this system.

00:12:04.940 --> 00:12:06.500
Uh, but those things are there.

00:12:06.680 --> 00:12:11.900
The other thing that is, like, interesting and different about that gun.

00:12:11.900 --> 00:12:20.400
And, I mean, one, you know, there's, like, the physics and, like, you know, the, since the bullets, quote, unquote, are these blobs, globs of ectoplasma or whatever slime, whatever it is.

00:12:20.900 --> 00:12:24.120
Um, it, it kind of goes in, like, an arc and, like, plops down.

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:25.660
It doesn't, like, shoot straight forward.

00:12:26.300 --> 00:12:33.140
But also, hitting up or down on the D-pad makes you aim up or down, but, like, on, you know.

00:12:33.240 --> 00:12:34.840
It's an angular aim.

00:12:34.840 --> 00:12:36.080
Yeah, it's various angles.

00:12:36.280 --> 00:12:42.120
So, like, if you hit up just once, you're gonna aim at, like, a, you know, at, like, a 45 degree angle, maybe even less than that.

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:45.120
And then, like, up again, and it's, like, you know, maybe a 70 degree angle.

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:46.700
Then you're, like, right at a 90 degree angle.

00:12:46.900 --> 00:12:50.360
And, like, that gets a little weird.

00:12:50.940 --> 00:12:51.960
It's a little overwhelming.

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:54.180
Gameplay-wise. Yeah. Yeah, yeah, definitely.

00:12:54.600 --> 00:12:59.720
But, yeah, you can, and, like, I find myself, honestly, mostly just aiming at, like, a 45 degree angle.

00:13:00.360 --> 00:13:02.460
Because, like, most of the enemies come from above.

00:13:02.620 --> 00:13:04.200
And it's just easier to stay like that.

00:13:04.280 --> 00:13:06.480
Like, that be my default rather than shooting forward.

00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:08.620
Yeah. But, yeah, it was interesting.

00:13:08.920 --> 00:13:14.420
It's weird that they chose to lock it in so that you have to change the direction via button input.

00:13:14.420 --> 00:13:23.040
Where we've seen games like Contra successfully do this, you know, much easier and much more freeing.

00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:29.400
And I can't help but feel like, you know, yeah, Contra had a lot more enemies and a lot more of, like, a closed-in space.

00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:32.340
So, you know, you did need to be more reactive.

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:37.820
But we're just being hampered by not being able to do that in this game, having already seen it be done.

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:40.040
Now, what do you mean by that?

00:13:40.100 --> 00:13:47.540
You mean the fact that if you let go, it doesn't, like, default to a default angle?

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:55.980
Yes, exactly. And, like, that you can just, like, you know, in Contra, you can just shift to the exact direction that you need to be in.

00:13:55.980 --> 00:13:59.380
So you can jump all the way to the other diagonal end of yourself.

00:13:59.720 --> 00:14:07.360
Yeah. They seem to have prioritized being very, like, being very exact.

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:12.640
And, you know, in Contra, you only have, what, like, eight directions to shoot in?

00:14:12.960 --> 00:14:17.380
Correct. And this one, there's, like, probably 16 or 32 directions you can shoot in.

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:21.840
I don't really understand why those are all there, but they seem to prioritize that.

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:27.200
All right.

00:14:43.920 --> 00:14:54.080
Just to jump in for a second, just to show you how much we know versus how much Ghostbusters fans know versus how much Activision the makers of this game knew about Ghostbusters,

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:59.060
the Ghostbusters 2 manual referred to it as the slime blower.

00:14:59.320 --> 00:15:02.160
But we all, including me, Sean, and Joe, we knew this.

00:15:02.160 --> 00:15:04.340
We just didn't know it because we're not super fans.

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:08.640
But when I say it, the thing is referred to as the proton pack.

00:15:08.960 --> 00:15:10.620
That is the official name.

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:12.160
And everybody knows that.

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:15.460
Yeah. It's just we didn't, you know, we're not that big of it.

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:17.020
But, like, that is weird, right?

00:15:17.420 --> 00:15:18.600
Yeah. It is strange.

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:24.860
To call it the slime blower and never say, like, were they not able to get the right proton pack?

00:15:25.120 --> 00:15:30.180
Yeah, exactly. The entire IP of Ghostbusters, except for proton pack, they were able to license.

00:15:30.600 --> 00:15:32.300
That's extra. That's strange.

00:15:32.520 --> 00:15:50.320
Yeah. But there's, you know, the issue also with the ghostbusting part of the game is that there are a lot of different things going on at different planes of the screen with no real need to engage with any of them when your goal is to just get to the end of the stage.

00:15:50.480 --> 00:15:52.020
Like, yeah, it's nice to get points.

00:15:52.240 --> 00:15:58.220
Yeah, it's nice to get those Ghostbusters logos, which are, you know, it's kind of meta that they're all over the place.

00:15:58.340 --> 00:16:00.320
But collecting those is good for you.

00:16:00.320 --> 00:16:08.240
So, otherwise, it's just in your best interest to dodge and not necessarily slime and destroy things, correct?

00:16:08.840 --> 00:16:10.340
Yeah. I mean, you're gonna...

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:13.240
Like, you've got to do it, but not for everything.

00:16:13.520 --> 00:16:17.560
Yeah, it's more, I think, you're using it more as sort of crowd control.

00:16:17.820 --> 00:16:19.880
Like, you're trying to, you know, clear a path.

00:16:20.460 --> 00:16:37.420
Also, it's just fun to shoot the thing, and every once in a while when you see a particularly, like, dense area or a obstacle that you prefer to just get out of the way, then you can drop the Roomba down.

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:43.300
Yeah, it's definitely not a game where you are compelled to kill everything.

00:16:44.040 --> 00:16:47.220
Yeah, I mean, I use it specifically for, like, defense.

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:51.200
And, you know, I actually don't find it particularly fun to shoot it.

00:16:51.300 --> 00:16:52.680
I find it fun and...

00:16:52.680 --> 00:16:56.340
I find it interesting to shoot it, but, like, I find it kind of annoying.

00:16:57.180 --> 00:17:01.280
Because, like, sometimes I just need to kill something and it's, like, not that easy to aim.

00:17:01.860 --> 00:17:07.000
Especially because it arcs and because, like, yeah, the way you have to adjust the angle.

00:17:07.220 --> 00:17:14.400
I just think, like, even in this second stage of when you're ghostbusting, I'm not sure if it's supposed to be a library or a museum.

00:17:14.620 --> 00:17:19.600
But there are just enemies with patterns that are just kind of...

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:24.560
They're the slimes that are kind of sluggish but move diagonally all over the stage.

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:31.580
Yes, they drop some slime, but as long as you're in front of them, they don't move fast enough to necessarily, like, keep up with you.

00:17:31.720 --> 00:17:33.160
So, again, just dodge them.

00:17:33.460 --> 00:17:40.400
And then there's other things that move in, like, crazy diagonal patterns but in an up-down position.

00:17:40.400 --> 00:17:47.920
So they act more like, you know, guillotines where it's, like, just don't get hit by them at the bottom and you don't have to worry about them either.

00:17:48.300 --> 00:17:53.440
It's just something about the lack of need to ghostbust bothered me.

00:17:53.440 --> 00:17:59.480
Well, maybe they're trying to say something, like, you know, ghostbusting isn't a necessity.

00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:06.480
Like, it's nice to be free of poltergeists and phantasms, but we should just live and let live.

00:18:06.820 --> 00:18:13.920
Yeah, and I'm not arguing for, like, the Luigi's Mansion approach either, like, that we needed to be, like, sucking up and capturing ghosts or whatever.

00:18:13.920 --> 00:18:15.820
I mean, that would have been fine, too.

00:18:15.820 --> 00:18:28.940
But even just as, like, your proton pack is your gun and you're defeating these ghosts, it could have been maybe a little more, like, how do I say this?

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:35.360
Like, the enemies, I guess, could have been a little more confrontational rather than just, like, littered on the screen.

00:18:35.360 --> 00:18:38.600
Yeah, there's no AI here.

00:18:38.720 --> 00:18:42.060
They're just patterns and you're supposed to avoid or eliminate them.

00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:45.660
They're not trying to kill you.

00:18:45.840 --> 00:18:51.080
They just exist. Yeah, and otherwise there's really nothing else happening in the stage.

00:18:51.240 --> 00:18:59.440
So by just getting, by just continuing on in the direction you have to go in, which is a little weird because you're going right to left in a few of these stages.

00:18:59.440 --> 00:19:00.540
We haven't seen that, right?

00:19:00.540 --> 00:19:02.900
In almost all of them, you're going right to left.

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:03.820
It's very strange.

00:19:04.680 --> 00:19:07.800
I'm sorry. In the ghost busting one specifically, you're going right to left.

00:19:07.860 --> 00:19:09.720
Yes. But then in the car, you're going left to right.

00:19:09.940 --> 00:19:11.760
So are you just going around in circles?

00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:20.240
No, never mind. No, I guess I'm just saying, like, there's no other, like, key objective story beat, right?

00:19:20.400 --> 00:19:23.640
It's just complete the stage to get to the next stage.

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:27.960
And maybe it needed a plot point or a boss fight.

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:31.140
I don't know. There's probably not enough bosses in Ghostbusters 2.

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:33.480
But that never stops some other video game.

00:19:33.620 --> 00:19:35.560
Yeah, they should have used more set pieces.

00:19:35.760 --> 00:19:38.580
I'm sure there were set pieces in this movie, even though I haven't seen it.

00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:44.860
And maybe they shouldn't be used in the way of, like, maybe walking up some stairs.

00:19:45.080 --> 00:19:50.660
But, you know, I know that later in the game, there's the Lady Liberty.

00:19:50.660 --> 00:19:51.480
That's a thing.

00:19:51.900 --> 00:19:53.160
We just need more of that.

00:19:53.360 --> 00:19:55.740
I mean, I know we haven't gotten into, like, the other modes yet.

00:19:55.740 --> 00:20:03.160
But it just felt like there wasn't enough or, like, I don't know, maybe we're getting ahead of us here.

00:20:03.240 --> 00:20:12.340
But there's something weird about, like, you do this back and forth between the gun, you know, the run and gun section, the car section, the run and gun section, the car section.

00:20:12.620 --> 00:20:17.720
Then there's, like, a really long time where you're the Statue of Liberty.

00:20:18.180 --> 00:20:23.340
Like, where I'm, like, to the point where I'm, like, I've forgotten that there's more to this game.

00:20:23.340 --> 00:20:25.180
And I'm, like, okay, is this just the rest of the game?

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:32.060
Like, longer than it took me to do those first, like, whatever, four levels, I'm playing as the Statue of Liberty, it felt like.

00:20:32.240 --> 00:20:34.740
And then there's just, like, one more regular level after that.

00:20:34.820 --> 00:20:36.400
And then you're done. It's just, like, wait a minute.

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:43.060
Like, what? It just feels not, like, I don't know, like, not designed by, like, a person.

00:20:43.060 --> 00:20:43.940
It just feels random.

00:20:59.020 --> 00:21:05.360
Let's move on, then, to that ectomobile stage where, you know, it happens several times.

00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:15.080
But basically, after you finish a ghostbusting scene, you then get to go into the ectomobile and drive to the next place you need to go do some ghostbusting in.

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:23.100
And the weird thing about New York City is that it has no traffic whatsoever.

00:21:23.860 --> 00:21:26.860
But, yes, the manholes are just as bad as you remember them.

00:21:26.940 --> 00:21:28.820
In fact, they're now man pits.

00:21:29.700 --> 00:21:31.320
Two things that just aren't true, right?

00:21:31.320 --> 00:21:39.560
Like, right now, I'm confused about the layout of New York City in this game because there's nobody else on the road other than a bunch of ghosts.

00:21:39.680 --> 00:21:43.100
So maybe the police managed to, like, I don't know, shut down all of traffic.

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:47.260
But then also, like, we don't have holes that large.

00:21:47.460 --> 00:21:51.800
Like, these are gigantic pits. No, you don't remember when Lexington Avenue turned into a giant chasm?

00:21:51.940 --> 00:21:56.860
Yeah, and it's like, I thought it would have just been funnier to do the manhole stuff, right?

00:21:56.860 --> 00:22:09.220
Like, to just comment on the infrastructure of the city instead of, you know, perfectly timing yourself onto these turbo pads that give you just enough boost so that when you jump, you perfectly cross these gaps.

00:22:09.220 --> 00:22:17.960
It feels like this went kind of zany where the ghost busting stages stayed more grounded in a weird way.

00:22:18.340 --> 00:22:20.460
Yeah, I don't really know what...

00:22:20.460 --> 00:22:26.900
I get that, you know, driving around the city is something that they needed to put in here.

00:22:27.100 --> 00:22:31.980
It's just, like, it's too iconic, I guess, if these two games are anything to go by.

00:22:32.900 --> 00:22:44.440
Anyway, so I get that that needed to be there, but I don't know what made them go this route with making it this outlandish because these are very hard levels, too.

00:22:44.940 --> 00:22:57.100
Like, this is almost like Battletoads on the jet skis in the sewers hard where I actually, like, got stuck several times because there were just the pitfalls I just couldn't jump over.

00:22:57.100 --> 00:22:59.820
Well, yeah, there's some, like, issues with...

00:22:59.820 --> 00:23:15.800
Not issues, but, like, you have to be very precise with the timing for those jumps, especially when there's, like, a speed boost that you need, then a jump, then a very small platform to land on with another speed boost that you also need to complete, like, more of the jump.

00:23:16.320 --> 00:23:21.480
So it's, like, you don't have really a lot of time to know that's coming or to process it before you have to do it.

00:23:21.700 --> 00:23:26.340
So, like, that was, like, a little bit challenging.

00:23:26.520 --> 00:23:33.980
But the fact that you could slow the car down made it a little more palatable, and I kind of liked the outlandishness.

00:23:34.140 --> 00:23:45.600
And I will say that I personally had not saying that I loved the driving section, but had more fun with this by far than the run and gun sections.

00:23:45.800 --> 00:23:47.680
I don't know how you guys felt. It's a lot more straightforward.

00:23:47.980 --> 00:23:49.740
I kind of agree with that.

00:23:50.660 --> 00:23:54.480
It definitely was just more difficult in my eyes.

00:23:54.640 --> 00:23:57.460
But, because, yeah, there's a lot going on.

00:23:57.560 --> 00:24:08.400
You have to navigate the screen itself, and then you have to manage the enemies that are popping up everywhere, also the obstacles, also the pitfalls.

00:24:09.720 --> 00:24:15.900
Both of these modes of play are incredibly chaotic, and everything is out to kill you.

00:24:16.840 --> 00:24:19.720
So, yeah, it's pretty unforgiving.

00:24:20.420 --> 00:24:29.140
Yeah, but the pace of play in the Ectomobile is completely jarring to the ghostbusting, where you had, like, it's up to you to get to the end, right?

00:24:29.300 --> 00:24:38.060
Now, instead, you're on rails, and it's scrolling pretty fast, and your turbo stuff is only going to make it faster, but it's necessary to get the turbo stuff.

00:24:38.280 --> 00:24:41.100
Right, yeah. And you have to get through here.

00:24:41.300 --> 00:24:46.160
Yeah. If you're not going fast enough, you're not going to progress.

00:24:46.820 --> 00:24:51.000
Right. So, there's just a, and it doesn't feel good to stop, either.

00:24:51.420 --> 00:25:06.800
But, you know, obviously on purpose, because it's not supposed to be rewarded, but it, like, doesn't feel good in the sense of, like, it completely kills any sort of cool moment you were having with the game of being in control of the Ectomobile in a way that I don't think really works in the game's favor.

00:25:06.800 --> 00:25:13.320
Because it's one thing to, like, basically, in order to have fun with this stage, you have to play it perfectly.

00:25:13.340 --> 00:25:14.480
And I think that's an issue.

00:25:14.820 --> 00:25:16.360
It's okay to make mistakes, right?

00:25:16.480 --> 00:25:18.640
Like, usually that's why there's health bars in games.

00:25:18.760 --> 00:25:20.700
It's like, you get hit once, you're not dead.

00:25:21.040 --> 00:25:23.500
You get hit a few times, now it's like you pay the price.

00:25:23.600 --> 00:25:32.120
It's like, with the Ectomobile stage, it's just frustrating that something that comes down to basically reflexes and not necessarily memorization.

00:25:32.120 --> 00:25:40.260
It's not like a Battletoads level of memorization, but, like, you know, you're doing this once, you feel good about it.

00:25:40.360 --> 00:25:42.480
Don't forget, you still got to do it, like, five more times.

00:25:42.660 --> 00:25:45.140
A movie tie-in should not be Ninja Gaiden.

00:25:56.260 --> 00:26:00.720
All right, so after the Ectomobile, now we get back to the ghost busting.

00:26:00.880 --> 00:26:08.840
We do that for a little bit, and then, as Joe mentioned, the game completely changes into a Statue of Liberty Galaga shmup,

00:26:08.840 --> 00:26:18.180
where you control the Statue of Liberty and you shoot, I'm going to guess they're like little balls of fire from the torch,

00:26:18.340 --> 00:26:24.140
out at the ghosts that don't, I don't know, they don't really look like ghosts to me.

00:26:24.520 --> 00:26:25.860
They look like seagulls.

